# Akahu API — ask the provider directly what it actually holds.
#
# Use with the VS Code "REST Client" extension (humao.rest-client), or copy any
# request into curl. Click "Send Request" above any ### block.
#
# Tokens
# ------
# Both come from https://my.akahu.nz/developers (Personal App tokens):
#   user_token  — the long token, sent as the Bearer credential
#   app_token   — the short app id, sent as X-Akahu-Id
#
# These two are the same pair Securo's connection is using, so what you see here
# is exactly what the sync sees. Do NOT commit real values: this file is a
# template, and a token in git is a credential in git.
#
# If you want the tokens this server already holds rather than re-issuing them,
# run this on the box and copy the two values out of your own terminal:
#
#   docker compose exec -T backend python -c "
#   import asyncio; from app.core.database import async_session_maker
#   from app.models.bank_connection import BankConnection
#   async def m():
#       async with async_session_maker() as s:
#           c = await s.get(BankConnection, __import__('uuid').UUID('5e98fd42-21d9-462d-8621-15dbf22e7d1f'))
#           print(c.credentials)
#   asyncio.run(m())"

@base = https://api.akahu.io/v1
@userToken = user_token~PASTE_ME
@appToken = app_token~PASTE_ME

# Akahu ids for the accounts in question. `Zero Visa` is the empty card; the
# other three came from the same (newest) Kiwibank consent.
@zeroVisa = acc_cmvoo2v7g000c02l28id8fyta
@wasteNot = acc_cmvoo2v6z000602l2amu04lne
@sambamajam = acc_cmvoo2v75000802l20nki6s9e
@savings = acc_cmvoo2v7a000a02l265nad8sg

@start = 2000-01-01
@end = 2026-10-27


### 1. Every account Akahu knows, with balance and refresh state
# Read `refreshed` on each item. A card that has transactions lists
# {balance, meta, transactions}; one that has never had them lists only
# {balance, meta}. That is the thing worth seeing with your own eyes.
GET {{base}}/accounts
Authorization: Bearer {{userToken}}
X-Akahu-Id: {{appToken}}
Accept: application/json


### 2. One account: balance versus refresh state
GET {{base}}/accounts/{{zeroVisa}}
Authorization: Bearer {{userToken}}
X-Akahu-Id: {{appToken}}
Accept: application/json


### 3. That account's transactions, ALL history (not a year)
# An empty `items` here, with a non-zero balance in request 2, is Akahu saying
# it holds the money but not the movements.
GET {{base}}/accounts/{{zeroVisa}}/transactions?start={{start}}&end={{end}}
Authorization: Bearer {{userToken}}
X-Akahu-Id: {{appToken}}
Accept: application/json


### 4. Same account, pending feed
GET {{base}}/accounts/{{zeroVisa}}/transactions/pending
Authorization: Bearer {{userToken}}
X-Akahu-Id: {{appToken}}
Accept: application/json


### 5. The workspace-wide feed — does the card appear anywhere at all?
# Count the `_account` values. If the card's id never appears, no parameter
# choice on our side could have found it.
GET {{base}}/transactions?start={{start}}&end={{end}}
Authorization: Bearer {{userToken}}
X-Akahu-Id: {{appToken}}
Accept: application/json


### 6. A checking account that does have history, for comparison
GET {{base}}/accounts/{{wasteNot}}/transactions?start={{start}}&end={{end}}
Authorization: Bearer {{userToken}}
X-Akahu-Id: {{appToken}}
Accept: application/json


### 7. How far back do the other accounts on this consent actually go?
GET {{base}}/accounts/{{sambamajam}}/transactions?start={{start}}&end={{end}}
Authorization: Bearer {{userToken}}
X-Akahu-Id: {{appToken}}
Accept: application/json


### 8. Kiwibank's account list as Akahu holds it (attributes tell you what was granted)
# `attributes` per account: TRANSACTIONS / PAYMENT_TO / PAYMENT_FROM.
GET {{base}}/accounts/{{savings}}
Authorization: Bearer {{userToken}}
X-Akahu-Id: {{appToken}}
Accept: application/json


### 9. Ask Akahu to re-pull from the bank now
# Akahu refreshes on its own schedule (roughly daily) and throttles this. The
# read that follows is what picks up anything new; the pull itself is async, so
# re-run request 1 a little later rather than expecting this to return data.
POST {{base}}/refresh
Authorization: Bearer {{userToken}}
X-Akahu-Id: {{appToken}}
Accept: application/json
